{"name":"Pickled Cucumber","hex":"#94a135","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pickled","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of pickle"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Preserved by pickling.","Drunk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pickled"},{"term":"cucumber","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vine in the gourd family, Cucumis sativus.","The edible fruit of this plant, having a green rind and crisp white flesh."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cucumber"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pickled cucumber","blocks":[{"text":"A pickled cucumber – commonly known as a pickle in the United States and Canada and a gherkin in Britain, Ireland, South Africa, Australia and New Zealand – is a usually small or miniature cucumber that has been pickled in a brine, vinegar, or other solution and left to ferment. The fermentation process is executed either by immersing the cucumbers in an acidic solution or through souring by lacto-fermentation. Pickled cucumbers are often part of mixed pickles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Pickle.jpg/330px-Pickle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pickled_cucumber","wikidata":"Q1365891"},{"title":"Pickling","blocks":[{"text":"Pickling is the process of preserving or extending the shelf life of food by either anaerobic fermentation in brine or immersion in vinegar. The pickling procedure typically affects the food's texture and flavor. The resulting food is called a pickle, or, if named, the name is prefaced with the word \"pickled\". Foods that are pickled include vegetables, fruits, mushrooms, meats, fish, dairy and eggs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Gherkins_and_Onions.JPG/330px-Gherkins_and_Onions.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pickling","wikidata":"Q1503967"},{"title":"Cucumber","blocks":[{"text":"The cucumber is a widely-cultivated creeping vine plant in the family Cucurbitaceae that bears cylindrical to spherical fruits, used as culinary vegetables. Considered an annual plant, there are three main types: slicing, pickling, and seedless."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/ARS_cucumber.jpg/330px-ARS_cucumber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cucumber","wikidata":"Q23425"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Pickled_cucumber.jpg/500px-Pickled_cucumber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Pickled_cucumber.jpg/500px-Pickled_cucumber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pickled cucumber in glass jar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APickled_cucumber.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/%E6%B5%85%E6%BC%AC_%E3%82%AD%E3%83%A5%E3%82%A6%E3%83%AA_%282710929826%29.jpg/500px-%E6%B5%85%E6%BC%AC_%E3%82%AD%E3%83%A5%E3%82%A6%E3%83%AA_%282710929826%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/%E6%B5%85%E6%BC%AC_%E3%82%AD%E3%83%A5%E3%82%A6%E3%83%AA_%282710929826%29.jpg/1280px-%E6%B5%85%E6%BC%AC_%E3%82%AD%E3%83%A5%E3%82%A6%E3%83%AA_%282710929826%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/%E6%B5%85%E6%BC%AC_%E3%82%AD%E3%83%A5%E3%82%A6%E3%83%AA_%282710929826%29.jpg/500px-%E6%B5%85%E6%BC%AC_%E3%82%AD%E3%83%A5%E3%82%A6%E3%83%AA_%282710929826%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Japanese asazuke pickled cucum